    "q-127705": {
      "dom_id": "step-q127705",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\sqrt{5},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=3t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, since $s=3t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{s\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s\\sqrt{5}}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-127705-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩",
